(Q6)Which command is used to modify file permissions in Linux? Give an example.
The chmod (change mode) command is used to modify file permissions in Linux.
Syntax:
chmod [options] permissions file/directory
Example:
# Give full permissions (rwx) to owner, read+execute to group and others 
chmod 755 file.txt 
# Give read+write to owner, read-only to group and others 
chmod 644 document.txt 
# Give full permissions to everyone
 chmod 777 script.sh
 # Give read+write+execute to owner only 
chmod 700 private_file.txt 
# Remove all permissions for group and others 
chmod 600 secret.txt
